# HDR-OUTPUT: Mac EDR output (scRGB linear) as UE r.HDR.*; Display.Output in machine.json (Scalability panel -> Display, palette group "Display").
# p4: the output transform is ACES at the display's peak (Common/TonemapACES.glslh TonemapACESOutput: the SSTS
# shoulder re-targeted to Display.PeakNits / PaperWhiteNits; SDR = the same code at headroom 1).
# Logs to read in editor.log: "[Display] output ...", "[Display] OS: ... EDR headroom ...", "[Display] HDR rendition of the captured frame: peak ...".
# B16_Bistro_Street live: run_capped killed the editor (resident 6516 MB > cap 6144 MB) while loading — reported; the
# proof runs on the Desert project's Starter scene (sunlit sand + sky + sun disc: highlights above paper white).
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Дано run Display "Display: Output SDR_sRGB"
Дано run Display "Display: Peak OS"
Тогда 1_sdr кадр как до задачи (SDR-захват не изменился, тон не сдвинут); editor.log "[Display] output SDR (sRGB): format BGRA8_UNORM colour space SRGB_NONLINEAR"
Когда run Display "Display: Peak 1000 nits"
Когда run Display "Display: Output scRGB_Linear"
Тогда 2_edr editor.log output scRGB linear (EDR) peak 1000 nits, headroom 1000/paper white; "HDR rendition of the captured frame: peak" well above 1.0 x paper white (sun/sky highlights reach toward the headroom, no flat clip); swapchain capture = SDR rendition; PNG matches 1_sdr; editor.log errors 0
Когда run Display "Display: Output SDR_sRGB"
Когда run Display "Display: Peak OS"
Тогда 3_sdr_back SDR again, same as 1_sdr (machine.json left at SDR, peak from the OS)
